  "title": "Third Plague Pandemic",
  "summary": "The third plague pandemic is dated to about 1855, when plague re-emerged from rodents in Yunnan, China. It travelled along trade routes to the coast, reached Canton and Hong Kong in 1894, then Bombay by 1896, and by 1900 had reached ports on every continent via steamship-borne rats.",
